Q17. Difference between JavaScript inside HTML and an external .js file.
Answer:

JavaScript inside HTML
JavaScript can be written directly inside an HTML file using the <script> tag.

<script>
    alert("Hello!");
</script>
External JavaScript
JavaScript can be written in a separate .js file and connected to HTML.

script.js

alert("Hello!");
HTML

<script src="script.js"></script>
Two advantages of external JavaScript:
Code can be reused across multiple HTML pages.

HTML remains cleaner and easier to maintain.

The provided notes demonstrate both inline and external JavaScript. 


Q18. Explain Frontend and Backend using the restaurant analogy.
Answer:

Imagine a website as a restaurant.

Customer = User: The customer interacts with the restaurant by placing an order.

