Section G: Higher Order Thinking
Q24. Why did JavaScript become so popular and multipurpose?
Answer:

JavaScript became popular because it started as a language for making webpages interactive, but its use expanded into many areas.

First, JavaScript runs directly in web browsers, so it became an important technology for Frontend development. It works together with HTML and CSS to create interactive websites.

Second, Node.js allowed JavaScript to run outside the browser. This made it possible to use JavaScript for Backend development, servers, and APIs. 


Third, JavaScript can now be used in many areas such as:

Frontend → React, Angular, Vue.js

Backend → Node.js, Express.js

Mobile apps → React Native

Desktop apps → Electron

Games → Phaser, Three.js

Data visualization → Chart.js, D3.js

Finally, ECMAScript provides the standard that defines how JavaScript should work. Regular ECMAScript updates have added new features over time. For example, ES6/ES2015 introduced let, const, arrow functions, and classes. 


Therefore, JavaScript became popular because it is versatile, cross-platform, continuously improved, and can be used across many types of applications.



